  {
    "source": "hn",
    "title": "Show HN: Build with Python – a beginner course where your code draws",
    "points": 40,
    "num_comments": 14,
    "url": "https://scimigo.com/en/learn/build-with-python/01-draw-with-python",
    "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49956771",
    "created_at": "2026-10-04T18:59:25+00:00",
    "story_text": "Hi HN, I built this because I watched my daughter struggle at learning Python. I made something that runs only in the browser with visuals rather than relying on CLI&#x2F;terminal output. No need to worry about python installation, package versions, venv etc.<p>The lab runs with Pyodide in a web worker, and the program output is a picture by the side of the code block. A user would experiment with the code, and see the immediate changes in the visual output.<p>The course has 13 modules, with the first 6 foundation modules free, module 7-13 with free readings but guide labs for a one-time price of $49.<p>Please give it a try at <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;scimigo.com&#x2F;en&#x2F;learn&#x2F;build-with-python\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;scimigo.com&#x2F;en&#x2F;learn&#x2F;build-with-python</a>\nSend me feedback on the UX and on the exercise design, especially if you teach kids to program.<p>I am also working on a C++ version for beginners (also with browser, no gcc or command lines). stay tuned.",
    "matched_keywords": [],
    "pre_filter_passed": true,
